# 必考词 Unit13
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-必考词
# 描述: 必考词Unit13核心高频词汇

{{inspect}}{/ɪnˈspekt/}}{v. 检查；视察}}{{Health inspectors regularly inspect restaurants for cleanliness.}}

{{inspire}}{/ɪnˈspaɪər/}}{v. 激发；鼓舞}}{{The teacher inspired her students to pursue their dreams.}}

{{install}}{/ɪnˈstɔːl/}}{v. 安装；设置}}{{They installed a new air conditioning system in the office.}}

{{instance}}{/ˈɪnstəns/}}{n. 例子；场合}}{{In this instance, the decision was made unanimously.}}

{{institute}}{/ˈɪnstɪtjuːt/}}{n. 机构；v. 建立}}{{The research institute published its findings in a journal.}}

{{institution}}{/ˌɪnstɪˈtjuːʃn/}}{n. 机构；制度}}{{Financial institutions play a key role in the economy.}}

{{instruct}}{/ɪnˈstrʌkt/}}{v. 指导；命令}}{{The teacher instructed the students to complete the assignment.}}

{{instrument}}{/ˈɪnstrəmənt/}}{n. 工具；乐器}}{{The scientist used a精密 instrument to measure the temperature.}}

{{insurance}}{/ɪnˈʃʊərəns/}}{n. 保险}}{{Health insurance covers most medical expenses.}}

{{intellectual}}{/ˌɪntəˈlektʃuəl/}}{adj. 智力的；n. 知识分子}}{{Intellectual property rights protect creators' inventions.}}

{{intelligence}}{/ɪnˈtelɪdʒəns/}}{n. 智力；情报}}{{Artificial intelligence is changing the way we live and work.}}

{{intend}}{/ɪnˈtend/}}{v. 打算；意图}}{{We intend to finish the project by the end of the year.}}

{{intense}}{/ɪnˈtens/}}{adj. 强烈的；紧张的}}{{The competition for the job was extremely intense.}}

{{interact}}{/ˌɪntərˈækt/}}{v. 互动；相互作用}}{{Children learn social skills by interacting with their peers.}}

{{interest}}{/ˈɪntrəst/}}{n. 兴趣；利益；利息}}{{She has a keen interest in environmental science.}}

{{interfere}}{/ˌɪntərˈfɪər/}}{v. 干涉；妨碍}}{{Please do not interfere with the investigation.}}

{{internal}}{/ɪnˈtɜːrnl/}}{adj. 内部的；国内的}}{{The company resolved its internal conflicts through mediation.}}

{{interpret}}{/ɪnˈtɜːrprɪt/}}{v. 解释；翻译}}{{Different people may interpret the same data differently.}}

{{interval}}{/ˈɪntərvl/}}{n. 间隔；间歇}}{{The buses run at 15-minute intervals during peak hours.}}

{{intervene}}{/ˌɪntərˈviːn/}}{v. 干预；介入}}{{The government intervened to stabilize the financial market.}}

{{intimate}}{/ˈɪntɪmət/}}{adj. 亲密的；私人的}}{{They had an intimate conversation about their future.}}

{{investigate}}{/ɪnˈvestɪɡeɪt/}}{v. 调查；研究}}{{The police are investigating the cause of the accident.}}

{{investment}}{/ɪnˈvestmənt/}}{n. 投资}}{{Real estate is considered a safe long-term investment.}}

{{invisible}}{/ɪnˈvɪzəbl/}}{adj. 看不见的；无形的}}{{The damage caused by pollution is often invisible to the naked eye.}}

{{involve}}{/ɪnˈvɒlv/}}{v. 涉及；包含；使参与}}{{The project involves collaboration between multiple departments.}}

{{isolate}}{/ˈaɪsəleɪt/}}{v. 隔离；孤立}}{{The patient was isolated to prevent the spread of infection.}}

{{issue}}{/ˈɪʃuː/}}{n. 问题；期刊；v. 发行}}{{Climate change is a major issue facing humanity today.}}

{{justify}}{/ˈdʒʌstɪfaɪ/}}{v. 证明...正当；为...辩护}}{{How can you justify spending so much money on entertainment?}}

{{keen}}{/kiːn/}}{adj. 敏锐的；渴望的}}{{She has a keen sense of observation.}}

{{label}}{/ˈleɪbl/}}{n. 标签；v. 贴标签}}{{Read the label carefully before taking the medicine.}}

{{landscape}}{/ˈlændskeɪp/}}{n. 风景；格局}}{{The digital landscape is constantly evolving.}}

{{launch}}{/lɔːntʃ/}}{v. 发射；发起；n. 发行}}{{The company launched a new product line last month.}}

{{layer}}{/ˈleɪər/}}{n. 层；层次}}{{The cake has three layers of chocolate and cream.}}

{{leadership}}{/ˈliːdərʃɪp/}}{n. 领导力；领导地位}}{{Good leadership is essential for a successful organization.}}

{{lean}}{/liːn/}}{v. 倾斜；依靠；adj. 精益的}}{{She leaned against the wall, exhausted from the long walk.}}

{{lecture}}{/ˈlektʃər/}}{n. 演讲；讲课}}{{The professor gave a fascinating lecture on quantum physics.}}

{{legal}}{/ˈliːɡl/}}{adj. 法律的；合法的}}{{The company took legal action against the fraud.}}

{{legislation}}{/ˌledʒɪsˈleɪʃn/}}{n. 立法；法律}}{{New legislation was introduced to protect consumer rights.}}

{{leisure}}{/ˈleʒər/}}{n. 休闲；空闲}}{{Reading is one of the most popular leisure activities.}}

{{liberal}}{/ˈlɪbərəl/}}{adj. 自由的；开明的}}{{The university has a liberal arts program.}}
